{"duration_api_ms":54528,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"34df02d4-4e9f-4747-bf12-dd98e6155079","total_cost_usd":0.18704380000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3928,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":7766,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7766,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7766,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":3928,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18704380000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"The Nimbrel Ledger append rejected with HTTP 429 document was authored by Priya Raghunathan.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Author: Priya Raghunathan\"},{\"text\":\"The Nimbrel Ledger append rejected with HTTP 429 document was updated 2026-03-18.\",\"line\":4,\"span\":\"Updated: 2026-03-18\"},{\"text\":\"Append requests to Nimbrel Ledger come back with HTTP 429 `Too Many Requests`.\",\"line\":8,\"span\":\"Append requests to Nimbrel Ledger come back with HTTP 429 `Too Many Requests`.\"},{\"text\":\"When Nimbrel Ledger appends are refused with HTTP 429, Nimbrel Relay stalls.\",\"line\":8,\"span\":\"Callers see a write that will not land: Nimbrel Relay stalls, batch loaders resend the same envelope, and reads against the same shard begin to time out.\"},{\"text\":\"When Nimbrel Ledger appends are refused with HTTP 429, batch loaders resend the same envelope.\",\"line\":8,\"span\":\"Callers see a write that will not land: Nimbrel Relay stalls, batch loaders resend the same envelope, and reads against the same shard begin to time out.\"},{\"text\":\"When Nimbrel Ledger appends are refused with HTTP 429, reads against the same shard begin to time out.\",\"line\":8,\"span\":\"Callers see a write that will not land: Nimbrel Relay stalls, batch loaders resend the same envelope, and reads against the same shard begin to time out.\"},{\"text\":\"The HTTP 429 append refusal reaches the client.\",\"line\":8,\"span\":\"The refusal reaches the client and is written to the Relay and Collector logs as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The HTTP 429 append refusal is written to the Relay and Collector logs.\",\"line\":8,\"span\":\"The refusal reaches the client and is written to the Relay and Collector logs as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The Nimbrel Ledger sends HTTP 429 replies when it refuses work rather than queueing it.\",\"line\":10,\"span\":\"On a managed Nimbrel Ledger deployment (NMD), HTTP `429` replies, which the Ledger sends when it refuses work rather than queueing it, can take a growing share of requests as counted at the front proxy; on one deployment that share climbed over a fortnight.\"},{\"text\":\"On a managed Nimbrel Ledger deployment (NMD), HTTP 429 replies can take a growing share of requests as counted at the front proxy.\",\"line\":10,\"span\":\"On a managed Nimbrel Ledger deployment (NMD), HTTP `429` replies, which the Ledger sends when it refuses work rather than queueing it, can take a growing share of requests as counted at the front proxy; on one deployment that share climbed over a fortnight.\"},{\"text\":\"On one managed Nimbrel Ledger deployment, the share of HTTP 429 replies climbed over a fortnight.\",\"line\":10,\"span\":\"On a managed Nimbrel Ledger deployment (NMD), HTTP `429` replies, which the Ledger sends when it refuses work rather than queueing it, can take a growing share of requests as counted at the front proxy; on one deployment that share climbed over a fortnight.\"},{\"text\":\"Where front proxy counters agree with the client reports, the HTTP 429 refusals are real and not a client-side accounting error.\",\"line\":10,\"span\":\"Where front proxy counters agree with the client reports, the refusals are real and not a client-side accounting error.\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, the append batch was refused after 0 of 64 envelopes.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, the error type is nbl_queue_refused_exception.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, follower_bytes=212992.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, all_bytes=88334336.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, ingest_op_bytes=155648.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"In the example refusal envelope, max_ingest_bytes=88080384.\",\"line\":15,\"span\":\"append batch refused after 0 of 64 envelopes: 429 Too Many Requests: {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"root_cause\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"}],\\\"type\\\":\\\"nbl_queue_refused_exception\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"refused append on ingest path [ingest_and_leader_bytes=88121344, follower_bytes=212992, all_bytes=88334336, ingest_op_bytes=155648, max_ingest_bytes=88080384]\\\"},\\\"status\\\":429}\"},{\"text\":\"The Ledger operations handbook covers refused appends under Refused Appends.\",\"line\":18,\"span\":\"> **NOTE:** The Ledger operations handbook now covers the same ground under Refused Appends, with a walkthrough for each of the three refusal paths set out below.\"},{\"text\":\"The Ledger operations handbook has a walkthrough for each of the three refusal paths.\",\"line\":18,\"span\":\"> **NOTE:** The Ledger operations handbook now covers the same ground under Refused Appends, with a walkthrough for each of the three refusal paths set out below.\"},{\"text\":\"Every Nimbrel Ledger release on every platform can refuse an append with HTTP 429.\",\"line\":22,\"span\":\"Every Nimbrel Ledger release on every platform can refuse an append this way.\"},{\"text\":\"Managed Nimbrel Ledger deployments are affected by HTTP 429 append refusals.\",\"line\":22,\"span\":\"Managed deployments are affected as well, for example:\"},{\"text\":\"The example affected environment runs Nimbrel Ledger versions 4.4, 5.x.\",\"line\":25,\"span\":\"Version: 4.4, 5.x\"},{\"text\":\"The example affected environment's platform is Nimbrel Cloud.\",\"line\":26,\"span\":\"Platform: Nimbrel Cloud\"},{\"text\":\"The example affected environment's deployment is Managed Ledger Service (MLS).\",\"line\":27,\"span\":\"Deployment: Managed Ledger Service (MLS)\"},{\"text\":\"The example affected environment is a production environment.\",\"line\":28,\"span\":\"Production Environment: Yes\"},{\"text\":\"A Ledger node sends a 429 - Too Many Requests reply once it has nowhere left to put the work.\",\"line\":32,\"span\":\"A [`429 - Too Many Requests` reply](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/http-status-codes) is what a Ledger node sends once it has nowhere left to put the work, which is to say once [an append queue or a read queue is full](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/why-appends-are-refused).\"},{\"text\":\"A Ledger node sends a 429 reply once an append queue or a read queue is full.\",\"line\":32,\"span\":\"A [`429 - Too Many Requests` reply](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/http-status-codes) is what a Ledger node sends once it has nowhere left to put the work, which is to say once [an append queue or a read queue is full](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/why-appends-are-refused).\"},{\"text\":\"There are 3 ways a Nimbrel Ledger append draws a 429.\",\"line\":34,\"span\":\"There are 3 ways an append draws a 429:\"},{\"text\":\"A Nimbrel Ledger append draws a 429 when the append or system_append worker pools hold more batches than they have slots for.\",\"line\":36,\"span\":\"The `append` or `system_append` worker pools hold more batches than they have slots for (`nbctl pool status --all`)\"},{\"text\":\"The command `nbctl pool status --all` checks the append and system_append worker pools.\",\"line\":36,\"span\":\"The `append` or `system_append` worker pools hold more batches than they have slots for (`nbctl pool status --all`)\"},{\"text\":\"A Nimbrel Ledger append draws a 429 when the ingest memory guard has refused the batch.\",\"line\":37,\"span\":\"The ingest memory guard has refused the batch (`nbctl guard report ingest --counters`).\"},{\"text\":\"The command `nbctl guard report ingest --counters` checks the ingest memory guard.\",\"line\":37,\"span\":\"The ingest memory guard has refused the batch (`nbctl guard report ingest --counters`).\"},{\"text\":\"A Nimbrel Ledger append draws a 429 when a circuit breaker has tripped.\",\"line\":38,\"span\":\"A circuit breaker has tripped (`nbctl breaker list --tripped`) - a breaker trips on any operation and is not particular to appends.\"},{\"text\":\"The command `nbctl breaker list --tripped` lists tripped circuit breakers.\",\"line\":38,\"span\":\"A circuit breaker has tripped (`nbctl breaker list --tripped`) - a breaker trips on any operation and is not particular to appends.\"},{\"text\":\"A Nimbrel Ledger circuit breaker trips on any operation and is not particular to appends.\",\"line\":38,\"span\":\"A circuit breaker has tripped (`nbctl breaker list --tripped`) - a breaker trips on any operation and is not particular to appends.\"},{\"text\":\"From release 4.6 and release 5.1 onward, appending to a wide_text column draws a 429 on its own account whenever the batch would otherwise have run the node out of memory.\",\"line\":40,\"span\":\"[1] **From release 4.6 and release 5.1 onward**, appending to a `wide_text` column draws a 429 on its own account whenever the batch would otherwise have run the node out of memory.\"},{\"text\":\"A refusal rate that climbs steadily can point at expensive queries and deep grouping.\",\"line\":42,\"span\":\"A refusal rate that climbs steadily can point at expensive queries and deep grouping:\"},{\"text\":\"A handful of queries run for as long as 2 seconds each.\",\"line\":44,\"span\":\"**Expensive queries**: a handful of queries run for as long as 2 seconds each.\"},{\"text\":\"A worker slot is unavailable for as long as an expensive query holds it.\",\"line\":44,\"span\":\"A worker slot is unavailable for as long as one of them holds it, and the queue behind it grows.\"},{\"text\":\"The queue behind a worker slot held by an expensive query grows.\",\"line\":44,\"span\":\"A worker slot is unavailable for as long as one of them holds it, and the queue behind it grows.\"},{\"text\":\"Grouping on channel.id yields a very large number of groups.\",\"line\":45,\"span\":\"**Deep grouping**: grouping on `channel.id` yields a very large number of groups, and the memory that costs is charged to the same pool the append path draws on.\"},{\"text\":\"The memory cost of grouping on channel.id is charged to the same pool the append path draws on.\",\"line\":45,\"span\":\"**Deep grouping**: grouping on `channel.id` yields a very large number of groups, and the memory that costs is charged to the same pool the append path draws on.\"},{\"text\":\"Processor load looks unremarkable while memory sits high.\",\"line\":46,\"span\":\"**Resource accounting**: processor load looks unremarkable while memory sits high.\"},{\"text\":\"Processor load and memory usage not agreeing points at query cost rather than at an undersized cluster.\",\"line\":46,\"span\":\"The two do not agree, which points at query cost rather than at an undersized cluster.\"},{\"text\":\"Taking append and query load off the cluster for long enough lets the queues drain and the nodes fall back under their limits.\",\"line\":50,\"span\":\"Take append and query load off the cluster for long enough that the queues drain and the nodes fall back under their limits.\"},{\"text\":\"Where batches carry wide_text columns and the cluster runs release 4.6 or release 5.1 or later, the workaround is to send fewer envelopes per batch.\",\"line\":52,\"span\":\"Where batches carry `wide_text` columns and the cluster runs release 4.6 or release 5.1 or later, send fewer envelopes per batch.\"},{\"text\":\"A cluster that refuses appends has been given more work than its hardware can carry.\",\"line\":56,\"span\":\"A cluster that refuses appends has been given more work than its hardware can carry, so the answer is hardware: larger nodes (scale up), or more of them (scale out).\"},{\"text\":\"The resolution for a cluster that refuses appends is larger nodes (scale up) or more nodes (scale out).\",\"line\":56,\"span\":\"A cluster that refuses appends has been given more work than its hardware can carry, so the answer is hardware: larger nodes (scale up), or more of them (scale out).\"},{\"text\":\"Per the sizing notes, scale up first in most cases.\",\"line\":56,\"span\":\"Scale up first in most cases, and scale out when what is wanted is a further copy of the data for availability, per [the sizing notes](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/sizing).\"},{\"text\":\"Per the sizing notes, scale out when what is wanted is a further copy of the data for availability.\",\"line\":56,\"span\":\"Scale up first in most cases, and scale out when what is wanted is a further copy of the data for availability, per [the sizing notes](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/sizing).\"},{\"text\":\"Splitting a hot stream over more leader shards spreads append load across more nodes.\",\"line\":58,\"span\":\"Splitting a hot stream over more leader shards spreads append load across more nodes, which helps in some layouts.\"},{\"text\":\"Splitting a hot stream over more leader shards helps in some layouts.\",\"line\":58,\"span\":\"Splitting a hot stream over more leader shards spreads append load across more nodes, which helps in some layouts.\"},{\"text\":\"For wide_text columns on release 4.6 and release 5.1 and later, the first step is cutting the number of envelopes in each append batch.\",\"line\":62,\"span\":\"Begin by cutting the number of envelopes in each append batch.\"},{\"text\":\"For wide_text columns on release 4.6 and release 5.1 and later, where smaller batches do not clear the refusals, add processor and memory capacity to the nodes.\",\"line\":63,\"span\":\"Where smaller batches do not clear it, add processor and memory capacity to the nodes.\"},{\"text\":\"For wide_text columns, raising the ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling cluster setting should come only after cutting batch size and adding capacity.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"Only then raise the `ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling` cluster setting, which defaults to 10% of the heap.\"},{\"text\":\"The ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling cluster setting defaults to 10% of the heap.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"Only then raise the `ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling` cluster setting, which defaults to 10% of the heap.\"},{\"text\":\"A higher ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling lets a node hold more in-flight append memory before refusing.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"A higher ceiling lets a node hold more in-flight append memory before refusing, and a node holding too much runs out of memory instead of refusing, which is the worse outcome.\"},{\"text\":\"A node holding too much in-flight append memory runs out of memory instead of refusing.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"A higher ceiling lets a node hold more in-flight append memory before refusing, and a node holding too much runs out of memory instead of refusing, which is the worse outcome.\"},{\"text\":\"A node running out of memory is a worse outcome than a node refusing appends.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"A higher ceiling lets a node hold more in-flight append memory before refusing, and a node holding too much runs out of memory instead of refusing, which is the worse outcome.\"},{\"text\":\"The ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling setting is read at startup.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"The setting is read at startup, so the cluster must be restarted for a change to take.\"},{\"text\":\"The cluster must be restarted for a change to ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling to take effect.\",\"line\":64,\"span\":\"The setting is read at startup, so the cluster must be restarted for a change to take.\"},{\"text\":\"Where scaling and setting changes are not possible, the load must change: fewer appends, cheaper queries, or both.\",\"line\":66,\"span\":\"Where none of that is open to you, the load itself is what changes: fewer appends, cheaper queries, or both.\"},{\"text\":\"Refusals that show up only during a spike usually clear on their own once the queues drain.\",\"line\":66,\"span\":\"Refusals that show up only during a spike usually clear on their own once the queues drain.\"},{\"text\":\"Where query cost rather than an undersized cluster is behind the refusals, the recommended action is to act on the queries.\",\"line\":68,\"span\":\"Where query cost rather than an undersized cluster is behind the refusals, act on the queries:\"},{\"text\":\"The recommended slow query threshold is 1 second.\",\"line\":70,\"span\":\"**Lower the slow query threshold**: set it to 1 second, so that the queries actually responsible are recorded instead of averaged away.\"},{\"text\":\"Lowering the slow query threshold to 1 second lets the queries actually responsible be recorded instead of averaged away.\",\"line\":70,\"span\":\"**Lower the slow query threshold**: set it to 1 second, so that the queries actually responsible are recorded instead of averaged away.\"},{\"text\":\"The recommendation is to go through the expensive queries with the team that wrote them.\",\"line\":71,\"span\":\"**Review what the queries are for**: go through the expensive ones with the team that wrote them, several of which look like they could ask for less.\"},{\"text\":\"While the refusal rate is high, the recommendation is to take a thread dump and a heap snapshot rather than reasoning from counters alone.\",\"line\":72,\"span\":\"**Capture evidence during a refusal**: while the refusal rate is high, take a thread dump and a heap snapshot rather than reasoning from counters alone.\"},{\"text\":\"The internal ticket for this issue is NB-40917.\",\"line\":78,\"span\":\"[Internal ticket NB-40917](https://tickets.nimbrel.example/issues/40917)\"}]}","ttft_ms":54551,"type":"result","duration_ms":54591,"uuid":"31f4cb1e-d35a-480f-9954-aef810e13d82","ttft_stream_ms":1661,"time_to_request_ms":106,"first_content_frame_ms":1661,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
